---
description: Dependency and external-resource policy. Stops new packages, CDNs and third-party scripts.
alwaysApply: true
---

# No new dependencies without approval

- Allowed packages: `astro`, `@astrojs/sitemap`. That's the full list.
- Before adding anything else (npm package, Astro integration, PostCSS plugin, icon set), STOP. Don't install it. Report the name, why it's needed and the plain-CSS/Astro alternative you considered.
- No external scripts, stylesheets or fonts from CDNs. Self-host everything under `public/`.
- No trackers or analytics in code. Cloudflare Web Analytics gets turned on in the Cloudflare dashboard at deploy time.
- No new config files beyond `astro.config.mjs`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json` and `tsconfig.json` unless the prompt file names them.
- Never run `npm audit fix --force` or upgrade major versions.
